--REQUEST--
hover
--EXPECT--
```nvs
enum Core\Http\Method
```

The HTTP methods that a `#[Route]` can use and a request can have. There are eight, and `CONNECT` is not one of them. The safe methods come first. The four methods from `Post` on are the ones the CSRF check covers.

**Cases**

- `Get` — Reads a resource. It is safe, so there is no CSRF check.
- `Head` — The same as `Get`, without a response body. It is safe.
- `Options` — Checks what a resource supports. It is safe.
- `Trace` — Sends the request back to the client. It is safe.
- `Post` — Sends data and can change state. It is the first of the four methods the CSRF check covers.
- `Put` — Replaces a resource. The CSRF check covers it.
- `Patch` — Changes part of a resource. The CSRF check covers it.
- `Delete` — Deletes a resource. The CSRF check covers it.
